@title Cold Room B temperature alarm
@subtitle What to do when the alarm goes off
@author Depot Operations, Marlowe Vaccine Depot

kpi Safe range | 2 to 8 degrees C | Cold Room B
kpi Cold Room B | 12400 doses | must stay in range
kpi Backup Cold Room C | 9000 doses | room for stock moved from B
kpi Polar Service | 555-0190 | responds within 4 hours

!!! **Nobody discards anything.** Only the Quality Manager decides what happens to any lot.

# Alarm levels

- **Warning:** the temperature is above 8 degrees for 10 minutes.
- **Critical:** the temperature is above 12 degrees or below 0 degrees.

# First 15 minutes

1. **Acknowledge the alarm** on the monitoring panel within 5 minutes.
2. **Check the door and seal.** Confirm the door is fully shut and the seal is intact.
3. **Check the compressor.** Confirm it has power, and note the temperature shown on the data logger.
4. **Call Polar Service** on 555-0190. They respond within 4 hours.

# Moving stock

If the temperature is still above 8 degrees after 15 minutes, move the doses to backup Cold Room C, which holds 9000 doses.

- The remaining 3400 doses go into the 6 validated transport boxes with ice packs.
- Log every box on the transfer sheet.

# Quarantine and escalation

!!! **Nobody discards anything.** Do not throw away, destroy or return any dose. Only the Quality Manager decides.

- Any lot out of range for more than 30 minutes in total is quarantined.
- Tell the Quality Manager immediately.
- If the alarm is not resolved within 2 hours, call the Operations Director.

# Contacts

